</code></pre>
<p>Let’s now look into a more elaborate question. Let’s imagine that from our data, we wished to produce a ranking of genres by their IMDB scores. It turns out that this can be done in a single line in SQL, but we will build up to it step-by-step.</p>
<p>To begin, note that IMDB scores are in the table Movie, while genre labels are in the table Genre. These two are connected through the table Movie_Genre. Let’s have a look at some of these relevant pieces of information below:</p>
<div class="interactive-sql">
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb64"><pre class="sourceCode sql interactive code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode sql"><span id="cb64-1"><a href="#cb64-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="kw">SELECT</span> movie_ID, imdb_score <span class="kw">FROM</span> Movie <span class="kw">LIMIT</span> <span class="dv">10</span>;</span></code><button title="Copy to Clipboard" class="code-copy-button"><i class="bi"></i></button></pre></div>
</div>
<pre><code>movie_ID                                  imdb_score
----------------------------------------  ----------------------------------------
M0000                                     7.9
M0001                                     7.1
M0002                                     6.8
M0003                                     8.5
M0004                                     7.1
M0005                                     6.6
M0006                                     6.2
M0007                                     7.8
M0008                                     7.5
M0009                                     7.5</code></pre>
<div class="interactive-sql">
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb66"><pre class="sourceCode sql interactive code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode sql"><span id="cb66-1"><a href="#cb66-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="kw">SELECT</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="kw">FROM</span> Genre <span class="kw">LIMIT</span> <span class="dv">10</span>;</span></code><button title="Copy to Clipboard" class="code-copy-button"><i class="bi"></i></button></pre></div>
</div>
<pre><code>genre_ID                                  genre_label
----------------------------------------  ----------------------------------------
G00                                       Action
G01                                       Adventure
G02                                       Fantasy
G03                                       Sci-Fi
G04                                       Thriller
G05                                       Documentary
G06                                       Romance
G07                                       Animation
G08                                       Comedy
G09                                       Family</code></pre>
<div class="interactive-sql">
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb68"><pre class="sourceCode sql interactive code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode sql"><span id="cb68-1"><a href="#cb68-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="kw">SELECT</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="kw">FROM</span> Movie_Genre <span class="kw">LIMIT</span> <span class="dv">10</span>;</span></code><button title="Copy to Clipboard" class="code-copy-button"><i class="bi"></i></button></pre></div>
</div>
<pre><code>movie_ID                                  genre_ID
----------------------------------------  ----------------------------------------
M0000                                     G00
M0000                                     G01
M0000                                     G02
M0000                                     G03
M0001                                     G00
M0001                                     G01
M0001                                     G02
M0002                                     G00
M0002                                     G01
M0002                                     G04</code></pre>
<p>The fastest way to print genre labels along with an imdb score is using JOIN twice to connect the table Genre to table Movie_Genre, and the table Movie_Genre to the table Movie. We can do all of this in one query:</p>
<div class="interactive-sql">
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb70"><pre class="sourceCode sql interactive code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode sql"><span id="cb70-1"><a href="#cb70-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="kw">SELECT</span> genre_label, genre_ID, movie_ID, imdb_score <span class="kw">FROM</span> Genre <span class="kw">JOIN</span> Movie_Genre <span class="kw">USING</span>(genre_ID) <span class="kw">JOIN</span> Movie <span class="kw">USING</span>(movie_ID) <span class="kw">LIMIT</span> <span class="dv">10</span>;</span></code><button title="Copy to Clipboard" class="code-copy-button"><i class="bi"></i></button></pre></div>
</div>
<pre><code>genre_label                               genre_ID                                  movie_ID  imdb_score
----------------------------------------  ----------------------------------------  --------  ----------
Action                                    G00                                       M0000     7.9
Adventure                                 G01                                       M0000     7.9
Fantasy                                   G02                                       M0000     7.9
Sci-Fi                                    G03                                       M0000     7.9
Action                                    G00                                       M0001     7.1
Adventure                                 G01                                       M0001     7.1
Fantasy                                   G02                                       M0001     7.1
Action                                    G00                                       M0002     6.8
Adventure                                 G01                                       M0002     6.8
Thriller                                  G04                                       M0002     6.8</code></pre>
<p>There’s a fair bit going on with this command, so we may want to unpick it a little bit…</p>
<p>We don’t actually need genre_ID and movie_ID to be printed above (we just print them to clarify things), so let’s just remove them from the SELECT:</p>
<div class="interactive-sql">
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb72"><pre class="sourceCode sql interactive code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode sql"><span id="cb72-1"><a href="#cb72-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="kw">SELECT</span> genre_label, imdb_score <span class="kw">FROM</span> Genre <span class="kw">JOIN</span> Movie_Genre <span class="kw">USING</span>(genre_ID) <span class="kw">JOIN</span> Movie <span class="kw">USING</span>(movie_ID) <span class="kw">LIMIT</span> <span class="dv">10</span>; </span></code><button title="Copy to Clipboard" class="code-copy-button"><i class="bi"></i></button></pre></div>
</div>
<pre><code>genre_label                               imdb_score
----------------------------------------  ----------------------------------------
Action                                    7.9
Adventure                                 7.9
Fantasy                                   7.9
Sci-Fi                                    7.9
Action                                    7.1
Adventure                                 7.1
Fantasy                                   7.1
Action                                    6.8
Adventure                                 6.8
Thriller                                  6.8</code></pre>
<p>The above output thus returns a single line for each movie*genre pair with the movie ranking. What we want now is to aggregate across all movies within a genre to provide the average score. We can do this quite simply with a <code>GROUP BY</code> command, and the function <code>AVG</code>:</p>
<div class="interactive-sql">
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb74"><pre class="sourceCode sql interactive code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode sql"><span id="cb74-1"><a href="#cb74-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="kw">SELECT</span> genre_label, <span class="fu">AVG</span>(imdb_score) <span class="kw">FROM</span> Genre <span class="kw">JOIN</span> Movie_Genre <span class="kw">USING</span>(genre_ID) <span class="kw">JOIN</span> Movie <span class="kw">USING</span>(movie_ID) <span class="kw">GROUP</span> <span class="kw">BY</span> genre_label; </span></code><button title="Copy to Clipboard" class="code-copy-button"><i class="bi"></i></button></pre></div>
</div>
<pre><code>genre_label                               AVG(imdb_score)
----------------------------------------  ----------------------------------------
Action                                    6.23657042869642
Adventure                                 6.44135667396062
